Z||000000||84Bill||07-30-2001||09:02 AM||||MMMMWaahhahahahaha <BR>NBC did a report on street racing crack down on Delaware St this past friday night. It seems street racing has made a strong upward surge due to "The fast and the furious" Friday and Saturday the Philadelphia Police went out and BLOCKED off the streets to stop people from exiting (an old tactic from the 60's) and went down the line issuing several hundred 190 dollar tickets. Arresting people without drivers licnses and impounding improperly tagged and illegal cars and cycles. <BR>WOW what a windfall for the City.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||TRiAD||07-30-2001||09:58 AM||||I'm probably one of the more adamant people about stopping streetracing; but even I can see there's probably more people who were "bystanders" there than actual racers. <P>I'm not sure the "hang 'em all" policy is going to be effective. Maybe having an undercover officer go in and videotape them (and later confiscate the other camcorders there as well) so they would have some proof of who is actually racing and what cars they were actually driving would be more effective...<P><BR>My $.02  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
