Z||000004||lowfunds||07-30-2001||10:38 AM||||I seem to hear a lot about if you know how to drive your car its ok. Im not against racing don't get me wrong, but to think nothing bad can happen because the people racing think they are professionals is wrong. I can't condemn others for something I do, but I think racing with spectators on each side of the road with nothing protecting them is stupid. Anytime someone want to race me we have a straight country road that the two of us can settle our differences. Besides the whole point is that you and the person you race know who has the faster car. Fifty people don't have to be standing along the road to prove that. Besides if you are like me you don't want everyone knowing how fast your car is.||||reg||1
